@startuml
title III-07 - Customer shopping cart, ordering and payOS payment

autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Customer
boundary "Customer Portal" as Web
control "Order API" as API
database "CRM Database" as DB
participant "payOS API" as PayOS
participant "Payment Timeout Scheduler" as Job

== Cart management ==

Customer -> Web: Add, edit or remove cart item
Web -> API: PUT /api/cart
API -> DB: Save cart changes
DB --> API: Cart saved
API --> Web: Cart summary
Web --> Customer: Show updated cart

== Create order and reserve stock ==

Customer -> Web: Confirm address and payment method
Web -> API: POST /api/orders\n(cart, address, paymentMethod)
API -> DB: BEGIN transaction
API -> DB: Lock products and read current stock

alt Insufficient stock or invalid item
    API -> DB: ROLLBACK
    API --> Web: 409 OUT_OF_STOCK / 400 INVALID_CART
    Web --> Customer: Show checkout error
else Stock available
    API -> DB: Insert order (PENDING_PAYMENT)
    API -> DB: Insert order_items
    API -> DB: Reserve/decrease stock
    API -> DB: COMMIT transaction
    API -> API: Create unique numeric orderCode
    API -> PayOS: POST /v2/payment-requests\n(amount, items, returnUrl, cancelUrl, expiredAt, signature)
    PayOS --> API: checkoutUrl, paymentLinkId, status PENDING
    API --> Web: 201 paymentUrl = checkoutUrl
    Web -> PayOS: Redirect to checkoutUrl
    Customer -> PayOS: Scan VietQR or complete bank transfer

    == Return/cancel URL: display only ==

    PayOS --> Web: Redirect returnUrl/cancelUrl\n(code, status, orderCode, paymentLinkId)
    Web -> API: GET /api/payments/payos/return
    API --> Web: Display payment or cancellation result
    Web --> Customer: Show result
    note right of Web
      Return URL and cancelUrl are for display only.
      They do not finalize the order.
    end note

    == Webhook: source of truth ==

    PayOS ->> API: POST /api/payments/payos/webhook\nJSON payload + signature
    API -> API: Verify HMAC-SHA256 signature
    API -> API: Verify orderCode, amount and data.code

    alt Invalid signature or mismatched data
        API --> PayOS: HTTP 400 Invalid webhook
    else Valid webhook
        API -> DB: BEGIN payment update transaction
        API -> DB: SELECT payment/order FOR UPDATE
        API -> DB: Insert webhook event\nUNIQUE(order_id, webhook_type, gateway_reference)

        alt success=true and data.code=00
            API -> DB: Update payment PAID
            API -> DB: Update order CONFIRMED
            API -> DB: COMMIT
            API --> PayOS: HTTP 200 OK
        else Failed, cancelled or expired payment
            API -> DB: Update payment FAILED/CANCELLED/EXPIRED
            API -> DB: Release reserved stock once
            API -> DB: COMMIT
            API --> PayOS: HTTP 200 OK
        else Duplicate webhook callback
            API -> DB: No-op because event was processed
            API -> DB: COMMIT
            API --> PayOS: HTTP 200 OK
        end
    end
end

== Expired pending-payment cleanup ==

Job -> API: Run every 5 minutes
API -> DB: BEGIN cleanup transaction
API -> DB: SELECT PENDING_PAYMENT orders older than timeout\nFOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
alt Expired orders found
    API -> DB: Update payment EXPIRED
    API -> DB: Update order CANCELLED
    API -> DB: Release reserved stock once
    API -> DB: COMMIT
else No expired orders
    API -> DB: COMMIT
end

note over API,PayOS
  payOS has no separate Sandbox/Staging environment.
  Test with a verified account and a small real transaction.
  Keep PAYOS_CLIENT_ID, PAYOS_API_KEY and PAYOS_CHECKSUM_KEY
  on the backend only.
end note

@enduml
